  "description": "<div>\n<p>Find the largest number of cells in a path through <code>matrix</code> whose values increase strictly at every step. Each step moves up, down, left, or right to an adjacent cell; diagonal movement is forbidden. The path may begin anywhere.</p>\n<p>A strictly increasing step cannot revisit a cell. Memoize the best path starting at each cell to avoid re-exploring its neighbors. Return zero for a matrix with no cells, including an empty outer list or rows of width zero.</p>\n<p><strong>Example 1:</strong></p><pre><strong>Input:</strong> matrix = [[9,9,4],[6,6,8],[2,1,1]]\n<strong>Output:</strong> 4</pre><p>One longest route follows 1 to 2 to 6 to 9.</p>\n<p><strong>Example 2:</strong></p><pre><strong>Input:</strong> matrix = [[1,2],[4,3]]\n<strong>Output:</strong> 4</pre><p>Follow 1, 2, 3, 4 around the four cells.</p>\n<p><strong>Example 3:</strong></p><pre><strong>Input:</strong> matrix = []\n<strong>Output:</strong> 0</pre><p>No cells means no path.</p>\n<p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p><ul><li>0 &lt;= matrix.length &lt;= 40</li><li>If there are rows, each has the same width from 0 to 40.</li><li>-1000 &lt;= matrix[i][j] &lt;= 1000.</li></ul>\n</div>",
